From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:57:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 378/378] pinctrl: aw9523: do not set a default IRQ trigger

When the expander is described in the device tree with an interrupt
parent, gpiolib warns at probe:

  /i2c@1101c000/gpio-expander@5b: Ignoring 3 default trigger

With a firmware node, the default trigger is ignored anyway. Consumers
set the trigger when they request a pin interrupt, and
aw9523_gpio_irq_type() accepts IRQ_TYPE_NONE. Leave default_type as
IRQ_TYPE_NONE, as gpiolib expects for firmware-described chips.

Observed on the Gemini PDA station with the AW9523 interrupt described.
Not yet run on hardware with this change.
---
 drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c
index 02a24ac87..5ccacef1d 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-aw9523.c
@@ -824,7 +824,7 @@ static int aw9523_init_irq(struct aw9523 *awi, int irq)
 	girq->parent_handler = NULL;
 	girq->num_parents = 0;
 	girq->parents = NULL;
-	girq->default_type = IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_BOTH;
+	girq->default_type = IRQ_TYPE_NONE;
 	girq->handler = handle_simple_irq;
 	girq->threaded = true;
 
